  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nHigh pressure is over the Ohio Valley this morning and will\ncontinue to build into our area today through early Wednesday.\nThere are still some lake effect clouds and a couple isolated\nlake effect showers this morning lingering over far northeast\nOhio and northwest Pennsylvania. The flow aloft will shift from\nnortherly to more westerly today and a weak upper level ridge\nwill move over the region today into tonight. The lake effect\nclouds will eventually clear out later today. The rest of the\narea will see a very nice, sunny day with high temperatures in\nthe middle 70s to around 80 degrees. Quiet and fair weather is\nexpected tonight into most of Wednesday with high temperatures \na couple degrees warmer. A weak cold front will approach the \narea Wednesday night with scattered showers and storms moving \ninto NWOH by late evening. There is a severe weather risk west \nof our local area but that threat quickly diminishes Wednesday \nnight as those storms will weaken by the time they move into \nNWOH. The cold front will slowly move across the area on \nThursday. There will be a redevelopment of showers and storms \nalong and ahead of the front. The severe weather threat will \nvery low due weak thermodynamics Thursday. Drier weather will \nmove in behind the Thursday evening, but there could be a few \nisolated lake enhanced showers near the lakeshore Thursday \nnight.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2.. \nWarmer temperatures and more nice weather will return Friday \nthrough the weekend. High pressure will build back into the \nregion Friday and weekend. High temperatures on Friday will \nrange from the middle 70s to lower 80s. Mostly sunny and late \nSummer very weather will be around this weekend with \ntemperatures in the upper 70s to middle 80s. That very weather \nmay continue into early next week. The next chance for showers \nand possible storms will be early next week with another cold \nfront dropping through the Great Lakes region.",
